# Provider data — never committed. Rebuilt from the API by the daily refresh.
# See "Data and API access" in README.md: republishing it is not permitted.
data/**
!data/README.md
*.duckdb
*.duckdb.wal
*.parquet
*.csv
*.tsv

# Secrets
.env*
!.env.example
*token*.json

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# macOS
.DS_Store
# Generated from the provider exports. Rebuild it with scripts/draft-board/build_data.py.
scripts/draft-board/Data.gs
# write_atomic's temp file beside it, mkstemp(prefix=".Data.gs.", suffix=".tmp"), if a hard
# kill lands between the temp write and the rename.
scripts/draft-board/.Data.gs.*.tmp

# Browser-automation artifacts. Page snapshots capture account details, and
# this repo is public.
.playwright-cli/

# Mock draft reviews quote provider ADP and projected GP, and GAP + Adj Rank
# recovers ADP exactly (ADR-0006). check-no-data.sh does not scan .md under
# docs/, so this entry is the guard. The procedure that generates them carries
# no numbers and is committed: docs/draft-board/mock-draft-review.md
docs/reviews/mock-drafts/
# Same content, second location. A report written to docs/mock-drafts/ was sitting
# untracked and uncovered: one glob per directory is one glob per way to get this wrong.
docs/mock-drafts/
# Generated studies over the local board (ADR-0026). A study reads the snapshot and renders
# aggregate counts, which are not provider data -- but check-no-data.sh does not scan .md or
# .html under docs/, so the directory is the guard, as it is for the mock-draft reviews
# above. The committed, reproducible artifact is the script that writes these:
# scripts/draft-board/study_*.py, with tests over synthetic fixtures.
docs/studies/
